# UNIT FORGE — master prompt

> One unit in, three artefacts out. Grounded, hour-allocated, and research-instrumented.
> Prerequisites: [`grounding/README.mdc`](./grounding/README.mdc) (evidence matrix) · [`.cursor/rules/lesson-publishing-integrity.mdc`](../.cursor/rules/lesson-publishing-integrity.mdc) (publishing rules) · [`fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc`](./fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc) (why the instruments exist)

---

## 0. Architecture — three logics, kept apart

A product-owner separation. Blurring these is the failure mode this document exists to prevent.

| Logic             | Owns                                                              | Unit of work       | Never                            |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| **L1 · Teaching** | Lesson, lab, exercises; hours; assessment                         | The **unit**       | Bent to suit a measurement       |
| **L2 · Research** | Consent, instruments, data custody, analysis                      | The **cohort**     | Allowed to change what is taught |
| **L3 · Product**  | The shared artefact (vShowroom) — backlog, architecture, releases | The **repository** | Confused with a grade            |

**Dependency direction is one-way:** L1 produces evidence → L2 observes it → L3 is where L1's lab hours land. **L2 never reaches back into L1.**

---

## 1. The CV definition — what "lesson, practice, lab" officially means

From the official Guía Docente (`desarrollo-web-front-end-i-2025-2026.json`, `formative_activities`), quoted because the distinctions are load-bearing:

| Type                         | Hours    | Official definition (abridged)                                                                                                                                | Forge output                                                  |
| ---------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Lección Magistral**        | **10 h** | _"Sesiones donde el profesor de forma expositiva presenta un contenido concreto… Tras la exposición suele haber un período de explicación de dudas o debate"_ | **Deck** (reveal.js) + the conceptual half of the lesson page |
| **Prácticas de Laboratorio** | **30 h** | _"…problemas de resolución práctica… por grupos o de forma individual… ejercicios prácticos en un **entorno similar al laboral**"_                            | **Lab brief** — team work on the shared repo                  |
| **Resolución de Ejercicios** | **14 h** | _"…problemas… **no necesariamente contextualizados al ámbito profesional**… adquisición y aplicación de estrategias de resolución"_                           | **Exercise set** — individual, decontextualised drills        |
| _Estudio autónomo_           | 94 h     | student's own study                                                                                                                                           | reading list + self-check                                     |
| _Evaluación_                 | 2 h      | the exam moment                                                                                                                                               | —                                                             |

**The distinction the official text makes, and the forge must honour:** the **lab is workplace-like and contextualised**; the **exercises are deliberately not**. One rehearses professional practice, the other isolates a strategy. They are not interchangeable, and a unit that only has lab work is out of compliance.

> ⚠️ **Current defect:** `tracks.yml` allocates only `duration` and `labHours`. **Lección Magistral (10 h) and Resolución de Ejercicios (14 h) are unallocated per session** — IGNITOR rule 2b covered lab hours only. Every forged unit must emit all three, and the totals must close at 10 / 30 / 14.

