## 2. Why the triad is also the research design

This is the elegant part, and it is not a coincidence — the official categories already separate the two things a small-cohort study must distinguish:

| Activity        | Work mode                        | Evidence produced                                        | Answers                                     |
| --------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| **Laboratorio** | **Team**, on the shared repo     | commits, PRs, AI-review accept/reject logs, release tags | _Did the cohort ship, and how did it work?_ |
| **Ejercicios**  | **Individual**, decontextualised | worked solutions, strategy traces                        | _Does this person understand it unaided?_   |

With **n < 15** you cannot separate "the team delivered" from "this student learned" by statistics. **The hour structure separates them by design.** Lab evidence is cohort-level; exercise evidence is individual-level; the oral defence (Unit 12) triangulates the two.

